A small PETSc subset for xv6 user programs: parallel AIJ matrices and
vectors assembled from COO entries, ghosted vectors, scatter-to-all, and
KSP (GMRES, CG, Richardson, PREONLY) with PC (ASM, BJACOBI, JACOBI, LU,
NONE), over the single-node MPI subset in user/mpi.c.

It implements the calls the fem port (user/fem) makes, with PETSc's
semantics where they matter (ownership layout, COO summation, ghost
updates, convergence test and reason codes).  ASM/BJACOBI subdomain
problems are solved exactly by the band LU in user/sparse/bandlu.hpp; real
PETSc uses ILU(0) there by default.  See doc/readme/readme_fem.md.

This is not PETSc and contains no PETSc source code.

Diagnostics: -ksp_trace prints each GMRES step per rank (basis vectors,
received off-process entries, local and reduced dot products, true
residual) through PetscSynchronizedPrintf/PetscSynchronizedFlush.
